{
  "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
  "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 1:00 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. CHAVIS: Mr. Chief Justice and may it please the Court: This case is about a logical reading of the statute's plain language, and section 3599(a)(2) that's printed on page 1 of the blue brief provides that when a state death row inmate seeks 2254 relief he shall be represented by counsel, he shall be appointed counsel by the federal court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We know that this means state clemency proceedings because of the words \"available\" and the words \"or other.\" For a 2254 petitioner or defendant like Mr. Harbison, the only type of clemency that is available to him is state clemency, and in order to give effect to the words \"or other\" that were used by Congress we know that that must refer to state clemency because the only type of clemency that the Federal Government provides is executive clemency."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why not? Why not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What would? Tell me, what would fall under \"all available post-conviction process\" in addition to clemency and competency proceedings?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, but he couldn't find it inappropriate, could he?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: I'm sorry. I'm sure I'm missing something here, because the statute does say \"all available post-conviction process.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0000-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: So you would interpret \"all available post-conviction process\" as meaning federal?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0000-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: But if it did not have the including phrase, if it just stopped there, would it then include proceedings necessary to exhaust the State remedies?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. CHAVIS: Your Honor, competency and clemency are in their own \"shall\" clause, mandatory clause, in and of themselves. They are not included in the -- the post-conviction process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "William M. Jay",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 3599 authorizes federally funded representation only in the three categories of proceedings specified in subsection (e). At least three distinct aspects of the statute's text and structure show that the only proceedings included are federal proceedings before a federal officer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Should the Constitution be amended it would cover that, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jay",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think that Congress intended to fund only those proceedings in which there are federal rights or federal interests at stake, and State clemency proceedings do not meet that qualification."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, you don't really think the fact that this provision was recodified helps your argument at all, do you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Clemency proceedings, judicial proceedings and clemency proceedings, we submit, are made clear by the text and structure of the statute to refer only to Federal proceedings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Clemency would be a particularly poor candidate for such funding because a clemency decision before a State governor, which may indeed be initiated before the -- before the inmate comes to Federal court for habeas petition, implicates no Federal rights and implicates indicates no Federal interests."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In particular in this case, the State of Tennessee takes no position, and at least four other times this statute has been litigated, other death penalty States have taken no position."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: How often has clemency been granted in Tennessee?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Chavis",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0003-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. CHAVIS: Your Honor, clemency has been granted one time since Furman, that I am aware of, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-8521",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "184a27e0e448b7b9c86109cf768d861ff1e556e1d01fc651a856295ff54dce97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-184a27e0e448-0003-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
